; Entity handler: patroller moving left (kind 2) and the tail shared by the movers that go left or up
;
; The handler of every enemy that walks or flies along a horizontal line: rats (room 2), red bats (room 8), worms
; (rooms 9, 14), skeletons (rooms 13, 22), crusaders (rooms 15, 20), red demons (rooms 21, 22), magenta flyers
; (rooms 20, 23) and the white ceiling ghosts of rooms 22 and 23. Which creature it is depends on the sprite description
; of its room record, not on the handler. A record of kind 2 starts moving left (this handler), a record of kind 3
; starts moving right (#R$B365); the two handlers turn the slot into each other at the ends of the patrol.
; .
; Handlers of the object slots are entered with SP at slot+2 (the RET of #R$A5E9 popped the handler word); they pop the
; words they need, push back the ones they change and end by jumping to #R$A5F0 with HL at the next slot.
; .
; The x coordinate goes down by the speed each frame. When its high byte equals the left turning point the handler
; word of the slot is rewritten with #R$B365, so from the next frame the same speed is added. The test is for
; equality, so a creature that starts outside its patrol (or a speed that skips a value) runs until x has wrapped
; round. The sprite is placed at (x, y); the hit box test and the drawing go on at #R$B2D4 (the first frame table of
; the sprite description, the one for creatures facing left).
; .
; Slot fields used: +2 word speed (8.8, 2-pixel units per frame), +4 byte left turning point of x, +5 byte right
; turning point, +6 word x (8.8; the high byte is in 2-pixel units, its low two bits are the shift phase of the
; sprite), +8 word y (8.8). The other fields are described at #R$B2D4.
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; SP Slot address + 2
@label=UpdateWalkLeft
c$B2A6 POP BC        ; speed
 $B2A7 POP DE        ; D right turning point, E left turning point
 $B2A8 POP HL        ; x (8.8)
 $B2A9 OR A          ;
 $B2AA SBC HL,BC     ; x goes left
 $B2AC PUSH HL       ; store x
 $B2AD POP HL        ; SP is back at slot+8
 $B2AE LD A,H        ; x in 2-pixel units
 $B2AF CP E          ; at the left turning point?
 $B2B0 JR NZ,$B2BF   ; no: go on
 $B2B2 LD HL,$FFFA   ; -6: back to slot+2
 $B2B5 ADD HL,SP     ;
 $B2B6 LD SP,HL      ;
 $B2B7 LD HL,$B365   ; from the next frame the creature goes right
 $B2BA PUSH HL       ; written over the handler word at slot+0
 $B2BB POP HL        ; pop the handler again
 $B2BC POP BC        ; pop speed, limits and x again
 $B2BD POP DE        ;
 $B2BE POP HL        ;
*$B2BF LD D,H        ; D = x
 $B2C0 POP HL        ; y (8.8)
 $B2C1 POP BC        ; skip the unused word at +$A
 $B2C2 LD E,H        ; E = y
; Entry point used by #R$B283 and #R$B436 (movers whose sprite faces left or up): D = x, E = y, H = y. Puts the
; position into the draw command and goes on to the hit box test with the first frame table.
@label=PlaceEntityLeft
*$B2C3 LD L,H        ; L = y
 $B2C4 LD H,D        ; H = x
 $B2C5 LD A,H        ; A = x in 2-pixel units
 $B2C6 EX AF,AF'     ; kept in A': its low two bits are the shift phase
 $B2C7 SRA H         ; x / 4: byte column
 $B2C9 SRA H         ;
 $B2CB LD ($ACD3),HL ; draw command position: (y, x/4)
; Entry point used by #R$B236: the position is already in the draw command. D = x, E = y, SP at slot+$C (the next words
; are the hit box). Tests the hit box against Jean and continues at #R$B2D4.
@label=TestEntityHitLeft
*$B2CE LD HL,$B2D4   ;
 $B2D1 JP $A851      ; #R$A851 tests the hit box, then jumps to the address in HL
